[Round 4/8 | Implementer | 117.4s | 0/400k] The baseline already has the core M2 ownership model: each MPSC slot owns a fixed `Box<[u8]>`, and enqueue/dequeue only copy bytes plus reset atomic metadata. I’m keeping that protocol and fixing the remaining initialization hole with explicit fallible vector construction. For throughput, I’ll also add a per-lane token-start cursor so producers usually find a released token without rescanning from token zero; token-state CAS remains the only capacity authority.

